WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.580
Two passages that are easy to mix up when reciting from memory:
Al-Qalam 68:15 and Al-Mutaffifin 83:13 are word for word the same.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:22.608
We saved notes on both while reading. Let's send them
to ChatGPT, and ask for a memory trick and a quiz.

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:31.808
Its trick is to remember the scene on either side: in Al-Qalam, a mark
upon the snout; in Al-Mutaffifin, hearts covered by what they earned.

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:42.008
It also flags an earlier overlap, muʿtadin athīm, found in both. From there
Al-Mutaffifin goes straight to the shared ayah; Al-Qalam takes two more.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:01:08.508
Then it tests us with five cards. Reciting Al-Qalam 68:15,
what comes next? 68:16, the mark upon the snout.

00:01:08.508 --> 00:01:23.508
Card two asks the same of Al-Mutaffifin 83:13,
where the answer is the covered hearts of 83:14.
